/--
Route-local low-gas frontier for the all-gas committed-safety theorem.

The high-gas side is checked replay.  Below the generated replay bound, the
missing proof should consume the concrete CALL response-safety carrier rather
than a bare `OpenXCommittedSafeBelow` oracle.
-/
def OpenXCommittedSafeBelowOfCommittedResponseSafety
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyCommittedResponseSafetyTraceReadyFor program targetProgram →
    OpenGasAware.OpenXCommittedSafeBelow targetProgram initial targetResult
      evmFuel gasBound

/--
Proof-friendly form of the response-safety low-gas frontier.

Instead of proving committed safety directly for every low-gas run, the future
induction can prove that each low-gas outcome directionally tracks some
reference result that already agrees with the gas-erased assembly result.
-/
def OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksOfCommittedResponseSafety
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyCommittedResponseSafetyTraceReadyFor program targetProgram →
    OpenGasAware.OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksResult targetProgram initial
      targetResult evmFuel gasBound

/--
Fixed-reference form of the response-safety low-gas frontier.

The future induction can pick a single reference result that agrees with the
target observation, then prove that every low-gas run tracks it. This avoids
re-selecting a witness per gas and matches an induction over one reference
open trace.
-/
def OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedOfCommittedResponseSafety
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyCommittedResponseSafetyTraceReadyFor program targetProgram →
    ∃ reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult,
      OpenGasAware.OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedResult targetProgram
        initial targetResult evmFuel gasBound reference

/--
Fixed-reference low-gas frontier against the trace-to-trace response tracker.

This is the shape intended for the low-gas induction: compare one reference
trace with the candidate low-gas trace. Ordinary CALL responses must strictly
track the reference response; the only asymmetric response case available to
the induction is all-forwarded child OOG, which should produce whole-run
failure tracking instead of a caller continuation.
-/
def OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedOfResponseTracking
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyResponseTrackingTraceReadyFor program targetProgram →
    ∃ reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult,
      OpenGasAware.OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedResult targetProgram
        initial targetResult evmFuel gasBound reference

/--
Trace-indexed fixed-reference frontier against the trace-to-trace response
tracker.

This keeps the low-gas candidate trace visible at the route boundary. The
actual induction can therefore prove tracking by constructing a candidate trace
and using `OpenXCallFamilyResponseTrackingTraceReadyFor` to relate its CALL
responses to the fixed reference trace.
-/
def OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceOfResponseTracking
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyResponseTrackingTraceReadyFor program targetProgram →
    ∃ reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult,
      OpenGasAware.OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceResult targetProgram
        initial targetResult evmFuel gasBound reference

/--
Trace-indexed fixed-reference frontier against the outcome-aware response
tracker.

This is a refinement of `OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceOfResponseTracking`.
Besides relating reference and candidate CALL responses, the carrier provides
the proof-facing fact needed by the all-forwarded-OOG branch: if a CALL success
bit differs, the candidate whole-run outcome is already classified as failure.
-/
def OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceOfResponseOutcomeTracking
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyResponseOutcomeTrackingTraceReadyFor program targetProgram →
    ∃ reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult,
      OpenGasAware.OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceResult targetProgram
        initial targetResult evmFuel gasBound reference

/--
Trace-indexed fixed-reference frontier against the result-tracking response
carrier.

This is the final-observation version of the outcome-aware frontier. A CALL
success-bit mismatch still forces the all-forwarded child-OOG certificate, but
the candidate whole run only has to safely track the fixed reference result:
it may fail/revert, or it may commit the same final observation.
-/
def OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceOfResponseResultTracking
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyResponseResultTrackingTraceReadyFor program targetProgram →
    ∃ reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult,
      OpenGasAware.OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceResult targetProgram
        initial targetResult evmFuel gasBound reference

/--
Trace-indexed fixed-reference frontier against the positive strict-or-exception
CALL response carrier.

This is the same low-gas obligation as
`OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceOfResponseResultTracking`, exposed in
the induction-friendly form where each CALL response pair is already split into
strict caller-visible equivalence or all-forwarded child-OOG plus whole-run
safe tracking.
-/
def OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTrackingTraceReadyFor program
      targetProgram →
    ∃ reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult,
      OpenGasAware.OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceResult targetProgram
        initial targetResult evmFuel gasBound reference

/--
Fixed-reference form of the strict-or-exception low-gas frontier.

This is the induction-facing version of
`OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking`.
The reference whole-run result is chosen once, while each low-gas candidate run
is still allowed to either fail/revert or commit the same observation.
-/
def OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceWithReferenceOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) (reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTrackingTraceReadyFor program
      targetProgram →
    OpenGasAware.OpenXCommittedSafeBelowTracksFixedTraceResult targetProgram
      initial targetResult evmFuel gasBound reference

/--
Exact-gas final-observation classifier for the strict-or-exception CALL carrier.

This is the low-gas proof target after collapsing observations to final committed
state/output and treating every revert/OOG as safe.  The successful branch only
requires committed-observation equality with the fixed target result, not the
stronger gas-aware replay agreement used by high-gas liveness.
-/
def OpenXTraceObservationOrFailureBelowOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTrackingTraceReadyFor program
      targetProgram →
    ∀ gas,
      gas < gasBound →
        gas < EvmYul.UInt256.size →
          (∃ candidateTrace : OpenExternal.OpenTrace,
            ∃ result : OpenGasAware.EVMResult,
              OpenGasAware.OpenXTraceResult
                (Assembly.GasAware.validJumps targetProgram) evmFuel
                (Assembly.GasAware.installCodeAndGas targetProgram gas initial)
                candidateTrace result ∧
                Assembly.GasAware.XResultCommittedObservation result =
                  Assembly.GasAware.XTargetCommittedObservation targetResult) ∨
          (∃ candidateTrace : OpenExternal.OpenTrace,
            ∃ outcome : Except OpenGasAware.EVMException OpenGasAware.EVMResult,
              OpenGasAware.OpenXOutcomeTraceResult
                (Assembly.GasAware.validJumps targetProgram) evmFuel
                (Assembly.GasAware.installCodeAndGas targetProgram gas initial)
                candidateTrace outcome ∧
                Assembly.GasAware.XRunOutcomeFails outcome)

/--
Universal low-gas safety target for the strict-or-exception CALL response
carrier.

Unlike `OpenXTraceObservationOrFailureBelowOfResponseStrict...`, this is not an
existential classifier that may choose one friendly candidate trace.  It says
that every candidate open outcome at every gas below the replay bound safely
tracks one fixed high-gas reference result, provided the CALL response carrier
relates ordinary continuing responses and routes asymmetric all-forwarded OOG
to whole-run tracking.
-/
def OpenXAllOutcomeTracesSafelyTrackReferenceBelowOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (evmFuel gasBound : Nat)
    (reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTrackingTraceReadyFor program
      targetProgram →
    ∀ gas,
      gas < gasBound →
        gas < EvmYul.UInt256.size →
          ∀ candidateTrace candidateOutcome,
            OpenGasAware.OpenXOutcomeTraceResult
              (Assembly.GasAware.validJumps targetProgram) evmFuel
              (Assembly.GasAware.installCodeAndGas targetProgram gas initial)
              candidateTrace candidateOutcome →
            Assembly.GasAware.XRunOutcomeSafelyTracks candidateOutcome
              (.ok reference)

/--
Universal low-gas final-observation safety for the strict-or-exception CALL
response carrier.

This is the final-observation form of
`OpenXAllOutcomeTracesSafelyTrackReferenceBelow...`: every candidate outcome
matching the response boundary either fails/reverts safely or commits the same
observation as `targetResult`.
-/
def OpenXAllOutcomeTracesSafelyMatchBelowOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking
    (program : Assembly.Program) (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram)
    (initial : EVMState) (targetResult : Assembly.StepResult)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  OpenXCallFamilyResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTrackingTraceReadyFor program
      targetProgram →
    ∀ gas,
      gas < gasBound →
        gas < EvmYul.UInt256.size →
          ∀ candidateTrace candidateOutcome,
            OpenGasAware.OpenXOutcomeTraceResult
              (Assembly.GasAware.validJumps targetProgram) evmFuel
              (Assembly.GasAware.installCodeAndGas targetProgram gas initial)
              candidateTrace candidateOutcome →
            Assembly.GasAware.XRunOutcomeSafelyMatches targetResult
              candidateOutcome

/--
Plain outcome-existence below a replay bound.

This is deliberately separated from universal safety: existence gives the old
angelic committed-safety witness, while `OpenXAllOutcomeTraces...` is the
demands-on-every-candidate part needed for the stronger safety theorem.
-/
def OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow
    (targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram) (initial : EVMState)
    (evmFuel gasBound : Nat) : Prop :=
  ∀ gas,
    gas < gasBound →
      gas < EvmYul.UInt256.size →
        ∃ candidateTrace,
        ∃ candidateOutcome,
          OpenGasAware.OpenXOutcomeTraceResult
            (Assembly.GasAware.validJumps targetProgram) evmFuel
            (Assembly.GasAware.installCodeAndGas targetProgram gas initial)
            candidateTrace candidateOutcome

namespace OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow

theorem to_openGasAware
    {targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram} {initial : EVMState}
    {evmFuel gasBound : Nat}
    (hExists :
      OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow targetProgram initial evmFuel gasBound) :
    OpenGasAware.OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow targetProgram initial evmFuel
      gasBound := by
  intro gas hLow hGasFits
  exact hExists gas hLow hGasFits

theorem of_openGasAware
    {targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram} {initial : EVMState}
    {evmFuel gasBound : Nat}
    (hExists :
      OpenGasAware.OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow targetProgram initial evmFuel
        gasBound) :
    OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow targetProgram initial evmFuel gasBound := by
  intro gas hLow hGasFits
  exact hExists gas hLow hGasFits

theorem of_openResult
    {targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram} {initial : EVMState}
    {evmFuel gasBound : Nat} :
    OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow targetProgram initial evmFuel gasBound :=
  of_openGasAware
    (OpenGasAware.OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsForAllGas.below_of_openResult
      (target := targetProgram) (initial := initial) (evmFuel := evmFuel)
      (gasBound := gasBound))

theorem zero_bound
    {targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram} {initial : EVMState}
    {evmFuel : Nat} :
    OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow targetProgram initial evmFuel 0 := by
  intro gas hLow hGasFits
  exact (Nat.not_lt_zero gas hLow).elim

theorem succ_of_at
    {targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram} {initial : EVMState}
    {evmFuel gasBound : Nat}
    (hBelow :
      OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow targetProgram initial evmFuel gasBound)
    (hAt :
      gasBound < EvmYul.UInt256.size →
        ∃ candidateTrace,
        ∃ candidateOutcome,
          OpenGasAware.OpenXOutcomeTraceResult
            (Assembly.GasAware.validJumps targetProgram) evmFuel
            (Assembly.GasAware.installCodeAndGas targetProgram gasBound
              initial)
            candidateTrace candidateOutcome) :
    OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow targetProgram initial evmFuel
      gasBound.succ := by
  intro gas hLow hGasFits
  by_cases hEq : gas = gasBound
  · subst gas
    exact hAt hGasFits
  · have hLe : gas ≤ gasBound := Nat.le_of_lt_succ hLow
    have hLt : gas < gasBound := Nat.lt_of_le_of_ne hLe hEq
    exact hBelow gas hLt hGasFits

end OpenXOutcomeTraceExistsBelow

namespace OpenXAllOutcomeTracesSafelyTrackReferenceBelowOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking

theorem mono
    {program : Assembly.Program} {targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram}
    {initial : EVMState} {evmFuel gasBoundSmall gasBoundLarge : Nat}
    {reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult}
    (hLe : gasBoundSmall ≤ gasBoundLarge)
    (hTrack :
      OpenXAllOutcomeTracesSafelyTrackReferenceBelowOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking
        program targetProgram initial evmFuel gasBoundLarge reference) :
    OpenXAllOutcomeTracesSafelyTrackReferenceBelowOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking
      program targetProgram initial evmFuel gasBoundSmall reference := by
  intro hStrict gas hLow hGasFits candidateTrace candidateOutcome hOutcome
  exact
    hTrack hStrict gas (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hLow hLe) hGasFits
      candidateTrace candidateOutcome hOutcome

theorem zero_bound
    {program : Assembly.Program} {targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram}
    {initial : EVMState} {evmFuel : Nat}
    {reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult} :
    OpenXAllOutcomeTracesSafelyTrackReferenceBelowOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking
      program targetProgram initial evmFuel 0 reference := by
  intro hStrict gas hLow hGasFits candidateTrace candidateOutcome hOutcome
  exact (Nat.not_lt_zero gas hLow).elim

theorem succ_of_at
    {program : Assembly.Program} {targetProgram : Assembly.TargetProgram}
    {initial : EVMState} {evmFuel gasBound : Nat}
    {reference : OpenGasAware.EVMResult}
    (hBelow :
      OpenXAllOutcomeTracesSafelyTrackReferenceBelowOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking
        program targetProgram initial evmFuel gasBound reference)
    (hAt :
      OpenXCallFamilyResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTrackingTraceReadyFor
          program targetProgram →
        gasBound < EvmYul.UInt256.size →
          ∀ candidateTrace candidateOutcome,
            OpenGasAware.OpenXOutcomeTraceResult
              (Assembly.GasAware.validJumps targetProgram) evmFuel
              (Assembly.GasAware.installCodeAndGas targetProgram gasBound
                initial)
              candidateTrace candidateOutcome →
            Assembly.GasAware.XRunOutcomeSafelyTracks candidateOutcome
              (.ok reference)) :
    OpenXAllOutcomeTracesSafelyTrackReferenceBelowOfResponseStrictOrAllGasOOGResultTracking
      program targetProgram initial evmFuel gasBound.succ reference := by
  intro hStrict gas hLow hGasFits candidateTrace candidateOutcome hOutcome
  by_cases hEq : gas = gasBound
  · subst gas
